Did you tell him that for years now

259
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:25,432
you'd been looking for him?

260
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:30,062
- No, I didn't.
- Why didn't you?

261
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:32,648
You're the only one who never gave up,

262
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:35,192
even after everyone else forgot
about him.

263
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:37,236
You should've told him that.

264
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:41,073
In any case,

265
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:43,575
I guess everything worked out.

266
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,411
Now that we know Jeong-yo is safe,

267
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:48,497
once he settles back in

268
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,290
and returns to his music,

269
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:52,709
you're bound to see each other.

270
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:00,592
So, when are you…

271
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,594
going to practice again?

272
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:09,101
Jeong-yo's back now  too.

273
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:11,228
Maybe you should just

274
00:21:11,895 --> 00:21:13,146
put your baggage behind you and--

275
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:16,358
- Are you here to lecture me?
- I'm just worried okay?

276
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:18,485
You've been gone for

277
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:19,403
a while now.

278
00:21:19,903 --> 00:21:21,363
And that's for me to deal with.

279
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:22,447
You still…

280
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:26,076
need time to figure it out?

281
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:42,592
SINHADAM

282
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:52,894
Get going.

283
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:01,278
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

284
00:22:05,073 --> 00:22:07,659
I'm the king of the world!

285
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:08,952
Woo, woo, woo!

286
00:22:49,368 --> 00:22:50,202
Choi Jeong-yo.

287
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:52,662
Be my practice buddy.

288
00:22:55,248 --> 00:22:56,124
What do you mean?

289
00:22:57,125 --> 00:23:00,420
Didn't you say you were busy prepping
for an upcoming competition?

290
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:01,713
No, I'm not going to enter any
competition.

291
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,840
I just want to practice with you and

292
00:23:03,924 --> 00:23:06,343
figure out a way to let music bring me
joy.

293
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:08,678
You can help me with that, right?

294
00:23:39,209 --> 00:23:40,085
Choi Jeong-yo?

295
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:44,840
Kang Pi-o.

296
00:23:50,679 --> 00:23:52,347
You said your name was Kang Pi-o?

297
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:54,766
That's what you said in Brno, right?

298
00:23:56,351 --> 00:23:58,437
Oh… Yeah.

299
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,108
When did you get back to Korea?

300
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:04,276
Not long ago.

301
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:06,736
I'm just here to take care of business.

302
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:11,408
- Why are you here at the school?
- Oh, uh,

303
00:24:11,491 --> 00:24:14,161
I looked  online and saw that I went here.

304
00:24:14,703 --> 00:24:16,037
Just thought I'd stop by.

305
00:24:16,955 --> 00:24:18,748
I have no idea where to go, though.

306
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:25,755
Are you here just to look around?

307
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:28,008
Uh. Uh huh.

308
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:30,635
- So--
- Real  quick--

309
00:24:32,804 --> 00:24:33,847
Why don't you go first?

310
00:24:33,930 --> 00:24:35,640
No, why don't you go first?

311
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:37,726
- Okay, should I then?
- Yeah.

312
00:24:38,226 --> 00:24:39,227
Um…

313
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:41,438
I'm really sorry about last time.

314
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:44,941
I was just on-edge and had my guard up
around strangers.

315
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:47,777
And I was exhausted from the competition.

316
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:48,987
I um…

317
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:52,115
I think I was pretty rude to you.

318
00:24:52,657 --> 00:24:53,742
Sorry for everything.

319
00:24:55,243 --> 00:24:56,077
No…

320
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:58,997
You don't have to feel bad about
anything.

321
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:01,208
Of course it would be weird for you.

322
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:07,422
Oh, uh…

323
00:25:10,133 --> 00:25:12,427
If, if you're still a little lost then

324
00:25:12,511 --> 00:25:14,179
I could show you around.

325
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:24,022
But seriously, what brings you to Korea?

326
00:25:25,106 --> 00:25:26,525
Oh, I uh…

327
00:25:27,275 --> 00:25:30,487
I was asked to guest conduct for the
Hankook Symphony Orchestra.

328
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:31,696
Really?

329
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,114
Yeah.

330
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:37,285
So are you…

331
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:39,829
are you going to do it?

332
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:40,872
Hmm,

333
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:42,541
I don't know.

334
00:25:43,750 --> 00:25:45,210
I still haven't decided yet.

335
00:25:45,835 --> 00:25:49,005
On one hand, it could be nice to
have a job in my home country.

336
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:52,133
On the other hand, it might just be more
confusing.

337
00:25:53,301 --> 00:25:54,135
So uh…

338
00:25:57,472 --> 00:25:58,557
Were we close?

339
00:26:00,141 --> 00:26:02,769
We entered the Harmonie Competition
together, right?

340
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:06,314
You went out of your way to find me so…

341
00:26:07,691 --> 00:26:10,110
I wondered if we might have been pretty
close.

342
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:13,738
I guess, yeah.

343
00:26:15,323 --> 00:26:16,908
I would say that we were close.

344
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:41,683
This is the classroom where we studied
together.

345
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:44,936
You transferred here midway
through the first year.

346
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:47,230
You were a "gifted scholar."

347
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:00,952
Where was my desk?

348
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:03,663
Right there.

349
00:27:11,838 --> 00:27:13,298
And where was yours, then?

350
00:27:16,259 --> 00:27:17,093
Here.

351
00:27:22,932 --> 00:27:23,767
Yes!

352
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:29,272
So do you recall anything?

353
00:27:30,523 --> 00:27:31,358
I don't.

354
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:34,361
I guess I didn't take school that
seriously.

355
00:27:36,571 --> 00:27:38,490
That's true, you didn't try that hard.

356
00:27:39,032 --> 00:27:40,784
Then what did I take seriously?

357
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:54,547
This is where you and I used to practice
four-hands together.

358
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:57,967
The thing you were most serious about
was the piano.

359
00:27:58,551 --> 00:27:59,886
Those practice rooms?

360
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,263
We basically lived in there.

361
00:28:11,147 --> 00:28:12,315
What piece did we play?

362
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:15,110
Do you still know it?

363
00:28:36,589 --> 00:28:37,424
My tendinitis

364
00:28:37,507 --> 00:28:38,508
it flared up again

365
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:42,470
- so playing the piano is uncomfortable.
- You're in a slump.

366
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:47,142
- No…
- How did you end up in a slump?

367
00:28:49,602 --> 00:28:50,854
That's not what it is.

368
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:25,597
You asked me before…

369
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:28,725
Why I ended up conducting instead of
performing.

370
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:30,935
Nine years ago,

371
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:34,731
I suffered a gunshot wound to the
right shoulder.

372
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:36,399
It was not the plan.

373
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:37,984
The plan

374
00:29:38,067 --> 00:29:40,987
was to let him go after we got the money.

375
00:29:41,696 --> 00:29:42,530
But

376
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:45,617
he put up a bit too much of a fight.

377
00:29:45,700 --> 00:29:47,827
It must've damaged the nerves
in my fingers.

378
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:50,830
I can go about my life just fine, I just
can't play piano.

379
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:53,750
And that's why I switched to conducting.

380
00:29:54,834 --> 00:29:57,170
But when I desperately want to play the
piano,

381
00:29:58,588 --> 00:29:59,798
I play this.

382
00:30:01,257 --> 00:30:02,759
While thanking Brahms for it.

383
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:13,812
I know how hard your predicament must be.

384
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:18,441
Take away music from a musician, and he's
left with hell.

385
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:20,443
As for your slump, well…

386
00:30:22,195 --> 00:30:24,364
You could overcome it with a little
effort.

387
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:27,325
But I can't.

388
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:32,372
To be honest, I'd say I'm jealous of you.

389
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:39,587
Thank you for everything today.

390
00:30:42,048 --> 00:30:43,049
Let's stay in touch.

391
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:50,473
Yeah. Get home safe.

392
00:30:51,599 --> 00:30:53,726
And let me know if you ever need
anything.

393
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:06,990
Nine years  ago,

394
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:10,326
I suffered a gunshot wound to the
right shoulder.

395
00:31:10,910 --> 00:31:13,663
It must've damaged the nerves in my
fingers. I can go about my life just

396
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:16,916
- fine, but I can't play the piano anymore.
- Was it for money?

397
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:19,419
Did you abduct him for that reason?
Or did  someone--

398
00:31:19,502 --> 00:31:21,462
Enough. You want to know?

399
00:31:22,505 --> 00:31:23,756
Three million lei.

400
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:24,883
Then I'll tell you.

401
00:31:26,050 --> 00:31:27,051
Where have you been?

402
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:35,059
Then you shall again discern between the
righteous and the wicked,

403
00:31:35,143 --> 00:31:38,313
between one who serves God and one
who does not serve Him.

404
00:31:40,481 --> 00:31:41,316
For behold,

405
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:44,402
the day is coming, burning like an oven.

406
00:31:46,070 --> 00:31:48,031
Says the Lord of hosts,

407
00:31:49,657 --> 00:31:50,992
"That will leave them with

408
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:52,368
neither root

409
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,371
nor any branches."

410
00:31:58,291 --> 00:31:59,125
You're home.

411
00:32:00,376 --> 00:32:01,836
Are Pi-o and Father home?

412
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:04,047
Mr. Kang isn't home yet,

413
00:32:04,130 --> 00:32:05,506
and Pi-o is in his room.

414
00:32:06,257 --> 00:32:08,051
Would you like me to prepare dinner?

415
00:32:08,134 --> 00:32:08,968
I'm not hungry.

416
00:32:18,436 --> 00:32:19,604
Ugh.

417
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:21,856
Pi-o.

418
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:25,985
What are you doing here?

419
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:27,528
Where have you been, Mom?

420
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:29,322
I was at church.

421
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:33,618
Yeah, I had… I had lector duty.

422
00:32:37,997 --> 00:32:38,831
So Mom…

423
00:32:41,709 --> 00:32:42,543
What?

424
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:45,713
That article about Jeong-yo.

425
00:32:47,006 --> 00:32:48,383
You've seen it too, right?

426
00:32:49,884 --> 00:32:50,718
Yeah.

427
00:32:51,344 --> 00:32:53,054
Yeah, yeah. I have.

428
00:32:53,554 --> 00:32:55,098
Gosh, I was so shocked.

429
00:32:56,265 --> 00:32:58,726
Still, thank goodness that he's alive.

430
00:33:01,646 --> 00:33:03,064
Are you planning to see him?

431
00:33:04,482 --> 00:33:05,900
I already did meet with him.

432
00:33:07,276 --> 00:33:08,152
Didn't know that.

433
00:33:09,153 --> 00:33:09,988
So uh…

434
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:12,407
Did he…

435
00:33:13,032 --> 00:33:15,034
- recognize you?
- No.

436
00:33:15,702 --> 00:33:16,828
He didn't remember me.

437
00:33:17,620 --> 00:33:18,454
Really?

438
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:24,627
Life is full of surprises but I never
thought something like that could happen.

439
00:33:25,503 --> 00:33:29,173
Still, from what I saw of his conducting,
he still has all of his talent.

440
00:33:29,924 --> 00:33:31,342
It's a silver lining, isn't it?

441
00:33:31,426 --> 00:33:32,719
"Silver lining"?

442
00:33:36,639 --> 00:33:38,349
Jeong-yo told me something…

443
00:33:38,891 --> 00:33:41,185
about why he's now a conductor instead.

444
00:33:42,061 --> 00:33:44,105
- Why?
- He suffered a…

445
00:33:44,605 --> 00:33:47,358
a gunshot wound to the shoulder
nine years ago.

446
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:49,527
So no.

447
00:33:51,654 --> 00:33:54,407
I don't know if I can really call that
a silver lining.

448
00:33:55,366 --> 00:33:56,200
Oh…

449
00:33:58,661 --> 00:34:00,246
I had no idea.

450
00:34:01,581 --> 00:34:05,001
But you know, plenty of people switch
from piano to conducting.

451
00:34:05,084 --> 00:34:06,252
Music is all connected.

452
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:07,879
It doesn't matter

453
00:34:08,588 --> 00:34:10,548
as long as you can make your own music.

454
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:13,384
Oh…

455
00:34:14,469 --> 00:34:17,055
I haven't done volunteer work like that
in a while.

456
00:34:17,138 --> 00:34:18,181
Good night.

457
00:34:34,155 --> 00:34:36,282
MARTIN VOGEL

458
00:34:38,743 --> 00:34:40,787
CALLING…
MARTIN VOGEL

459
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:50,713
Yo, Mr. Kang.

460
00:34:51,214 --> 00:34:52,882
Hey. You doing well?

461
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:56,552
Oh, uh, if you're calling about Mr. Choi,

462
00:34:56,636 --> 00:34:58,221
I don't have much to tell you.

463
00:34:58,721 --> 00:35:00,932
I mean we both heard that he's already
dead.

464
00:35:01,432 --> 00:35:02,266
No.

465
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:05,144
That's not the reason why I'm calling.

466
00:35:06,562 --> 00:35:07,438
What is it, then?

467
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:09,649
I have another favor to ask.

468
00:35:10,983 --> 00:35:11,818
What?

469
00:35:11,901 --> 00:35:12,860
I need you…

470
00:35:14,195 --> 00:35:16,781
to look into something and make sure
nothing leaks.

471
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,076
I want to know who the person behind…

472
00:35:21,577 --> 00:35:23,162
Choi Jeong-yo's kidnapping is.

473
00:35:34,590 --> 00:35:36,342
You haven't made your mind up yet?

474
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:38,970
No.

475
00:35:39,637 --> 00:35:40,471
I see.

476
00:35:41,889 --> 00:35:44,016
What is it that's making you hesitate?

477
00:35:44,517 --> 00:35:45,393
Our orchestra…

478
00:35:46,727 --> 00:35:50,523
You saw for yourself that when it comes
to skill, we come second to none.

479
00:35:50,606 --> 00:35:54,235
You'll be given the authority to appoint
and dismiss orchestra members; it's

480
00:35:54,318 --> 00:35:55,444
unprecedented control.

481
00:35:56,362 --> 00:35:58,030
So isn't this the best opportunity

482
00:35:58,114 --> 00:35:59,073
for your vision?

483
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:01,409
I guess it is.

484
00:36:02,743 --> 00:36:03,578
Let's talk pay?

485
00:36:04,495 --> 00:36:05,621
As far as I can tell,

486
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:08,708
what we're offering is relatively high, I
think.

487
00:36:10,376 --> 00:36:12,044
Does our offer need to go higher?

488
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:14,922
No. It's not about the money.

489
00:36:16,382 --> 00:36:17,216
Then what is it?

490
00:36:18,176 --> 00:36:19,802
What's preventing your decision?

491
00:36:22,471 --> 00:36:23,306
The truth is…

492
00:36:25,766 --> 00:36:29,770
the reason I wanted to come here was
to meet Maestro Kang Seung-woon.

493
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:33,816
I have a favor I want to ask him.

494
00:36:34,775 --> 00:36:36,235
What is it? You can tell me.

495
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:40,823
Oh.

496
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:44,911
You want to tell him directly
is that right?

497
00:36:46,954 --> 00:36:47,788
All right, then.

498
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:50,499
I'll arrange a time for you to meet
together.

499
00:36:51,500 --> 00:36:52,335
Okay.

500
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:56,005
Oh, you said you haven't chosen an agency
yet, right?

501
00:36:56,714 --> 00:36:57,548
Well,

502
00:36:57,632 --> 00:37:01,052
there's an agency I'd like to introduce
you to, if you're interested.

503
00:37:01,135 --> 00:37:02,637
Could I give them your number?

504
00:37:03,554 --> 00:37:04,388
What agency?

505
00:37:24,742 --> 00:37:25,576
Jeong-yo.

506
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,288
It's me, Hong Jae-in.

507
00:37:30,122 --> 00:37:30,957
So.

508
00:37:32,667 --> 00:37:33,751
Do you remember me?

509
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:36,254
Now that you've seen my face?

510
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:37,171
I don't.

511
00:37:39,090 --> 00:37:40,967
So you really have lost your memory.

512
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:44,178
Hm.

513
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:46,055
Still,

514
00:37:46,555 --> 00:37:48,474
it's a huge relief that you're here.

515
00:37:49,183 --> 00:37:51,060
You have no idea how shocked and

516
00:37:51,143 --> 00:37:54,605
how sad I was for the longest time,
thinking you were dead.

517
00:37:57,483 --> 00:37:59,485
- Sure.
- Hey.

518
00:38:00,319 --> 00:38:01,195
We're friends, okay?

519
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:03,990
You don't have to be so cold towards me.

520
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,118
Here.

521
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:10,871
This is that picture I

522
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:12,039
told you about.

523
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:14,250
Look at that.

524
00:38:14,792 --> 00:38:18,087
You can see how close we were. Just from
that photo.

525
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:19,797
Yep.

526
00:38:20,923 --> 00:38:21,799
It seems we were.

527
00:38:22,425 --> 00:38:23,259
Yeah.

528
00:38:23,843 --> 00:38:26,429
You were a really special friend to us.

529
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:28,389
That's why Pi-o

530
00:38:29,181 --> 00:38:30,725
couldn't give up on you

531
00:38:30,808 --> 00:38:32,476
and kept on looking for you

532
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:34,603
for years after you were gone.

533
00:38:35,521 --> 00:38:36,647
The only person who

534
00:38:37,148 --> 00:38:39,608
never forgot about you and kept on
searching…

535
00:38:40,484 --> 00:38:41,444
is your friend.

536
00:38:44,488 --> 00:38:45,323
Why though?

537
00:38:46,449 --> 00:38:47,491
Look at the photo.

538
00:38:48,576 --> 00:38:51,287
You guys… were the closest of friends.

539
00:38:52,872 --> 00:38:53,706
So uh…

540
00:38:54,290 --> 00:38:55,916
uh, the truth is,

541
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,919
there's a reason why I wanted to see you
today.

542
00:39:35,414 --> 00:39:38,376
BUSINESS PLAN AMENDMENT APPROVAL REQUEST
(APPOINTMENT OF PRINCIPAL CONDUCTOR)

543
00:39:38,459 --> 00:39:39,460
NCAPF STEERING COMMITTEE MEMBER
KANG JI-HYE

544
00:39:39,543 --> 00:39:40,378
"Luca Domenico"?

545
00:39:40,461 --> 00:39:43,172
AMENDED PLAN,
APPOINTMENT OF PRINCIPAL GUEST CONDUCTOR

546
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:44,090
Heh.

547
00:39:52,681 --> 00:39:53,516
Deputy Director.

548
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:56,727
What's this "Amendment Approval Request"?

549
00:39:56,811 --> 00:39:57,895
Oh, that.

550
00:39:58,437 --> 00:40:01,273
The Hankook Symphony wants to invite this
year's winner in Brno,

551
00:40:01,357 --> 00:40:03,859
Choi Jeong-yo, to guest conduct for them.

552
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:05,236
Well,

553
00:40:05,945 --> 00:40:09,031
this wasn't what we agreed to when we
approved the budget.

554
00:40:09,115 --> 00:40:12,076
They can't just suddenly request an
amendment like this.

555
00:40:12,159 --> 00:40:13,160
Uh…

556
00:40:13,244 --> 00:40:14,078
well, this is

557
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,122
standard procedure whenever a

558
00:40:16,205 --> 00:40:17,581
guest artist is brought in…

559
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:21,335
Also, Kang Seung-woon strongly
recommended him…

560
00:40:28,092 --> 00:40:28,926
Welcome home.

561
00:40:46,735 --> 00:40:47,570
Father.

562
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:49,155
Choi Jeong-yo…

563
00:40:49,989 --> 00:40:52,450
Did you have him invited to the Hankook
Symphony?

564
00:40:52,992 --> 00:40:55,536
- Yeah, what about it?
- Do you really not know?

565
00:40:56,078 --> 00:40:59,832
You've never paid attention to Pi-o, yet
the moment that kid shows up, you…

566
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,961
Do you not care about your grandson's
feelings?

567
00:41:04,044 --> 00:41:06,922
Why are you
playing the victim all over again?

568
00:41:07,673 --> 00:41:10,384
How are  you still  so  immature  at your
age, huh?

569
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:14,054
Why does  it have to  be him of  all
people?  Can't you  see

570
00:41:14,138 --> 00:41:15,931
Just how much Pi-o has suffered?

571
00:41:17,850 --> 00:41:20,269
You still don't see the bigger picture.

572
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:24,356
Your son wasn't actually hurt back then.

573
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:27,234
Choi Jeong-yo is the reason he was even
half decent.

574
00:41:28,068 --> 00:41:30,446
He was the only reason he won that
competition.

575
00:41:30,946 --> 00:41:33,199
How can you even say that you work in the
arts

576
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:35,242
without having that kind of insight?

577
00:41:35,326 --> 00:41:38,120
Pi-o won the competition entirely
on his own skill.

578
00:41:38,204 --> 00:41:41,040
Jeong-yo was nothing but a roadblock
in Pi-o's life.

579
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:45,211
I won't let my son get hurt like that
again so Choi Jeong-yo…

580
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:47,713
Forget about bringing him in.

581
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:49,882
Stop being unreasonable and get out.

582
00:41:49,965 --> 00:41:52,676
I don't have time to listen to you
throw fits.

583
00:42:05,981 --> 00:42:06,815
Ms. Kang.

584
00:42:06,899 --> 00:42:09,693
Yoon Seon-ju of the Hankook
Symphony Orchestra is here.

585
00:42:17,117 --> 00:42:19,203
Oh. There you are.

586
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:22,206
You wanted to see me, Ms. Kang?

587
00:42:22,706 --> 00:42:25,501
I'm sorry for making you come here
when you're so busy.

588
00:42:25,584 --> 00:42:27,920
I just…
I have so much work, I can't really

589
00:42:28,003 --> 00:42:29,505
leave my office.

590
00:42:30,130 --> 00:42:30,965
Have a seat.

591
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:44,770
I was looking over some paperwork for my
review,

592
00:42:45,646 --> 00:42:49,233
and I saw you were planning to bring in
another principal guest conductor.

593
00:42:49,316 --> 00:42:50,359
Now why would you…

594
00:42:51,819 --> 00:42:53,320
why would you want to do that?

595
00:42:53,904 --> 00:42:56,407
Is that something that really needs
explaining?

596
00:42:58,033 --> 00:43:00,995
You know who the conductor we're planning
to bring in is,

597
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:03,372
- don't you?
- Of course.

598
00:43:04,039 --> 00:43:05,165
How could I not?

599
00:43:06,500 --> 00:43:09,753
I was also grateful and elated to hear
that Jeong-yo was

600
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,422
alive and well.

601
00:43:12,673 --> 00:43:14,633
Then, I guess I don't need to

602
00:43:14,717 --> 00:43:17,011
tell you all about his star quality.

603
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:21,056
I think we should be commended for not
losing him to another country,

604
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:23,684
so we can strengthen Korea's music scene.

605
00:43:24,351 --> 00:43:25,811
Considering his prestige…

606
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:27,146
his salary

607
00:43:28,105 --> 00:43:29,315
would have to be higher.

608
00:43:30,357 --> 00:43:32,109
But if you insist on having him,

609
00:43:33,068 --> 00:43:36,614
I think we need to reconsider the subsidy
that we provide you.

610
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:39,033
Would you be okay with that?

611
00:43:43,579 --> 00:43:44,413
Why don't you…

612
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:48,083
why don't you like Choi Jeong-yo?

613
00:43:50,669 --> 00:43:52,338
What are you saying right now?

614
00:43:52,421 --> 00:43:54,173
I never said I didn't like him.

615
00:43:54,256 --> 00:43:55,215
Jeong-yo isn't

616
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:56,884
Pi-o's competitor any longer.

617
00:43:58,093 --> 00:43:58,927
Is there

618
00:43:59,803 --> 00:44:01,013
perhaps another reason--

619
00:44:01,096 --> 00:44:02,598
Look here, Ms. Yoon.

620
00:44:04,850 --> 00:44:07,770
Are you trying to make me out to be
someone who can't separate business and

621
00:44:07,853 --> 00:44:10,064
personal matters?
All I want to say is that…

622
00:44:11,190 --> 00:44:13,651
trying to chase after well-known
conductors like this

623
00:44:13,734 --> 00:44:17,529
does absolutely nothing to help develop
our classical music scene.

624
00:44:19,990 --> 00:44:20,824
Is that right?

625
00:44:22,701 --> 00:44:24,745
I guess… I understand now.

626
00:44:26,580 --> 00:44:27,414
What a shame.

627
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:31,627
At the end of the day, I'm a president
who can't turn down good business.

628
00:44:33,295 --> 00:44:34,254
It breaks my heart,

629
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:37,966
but we're going to pass

630
00:44:38,050 --> 00:44:38,926
on the subsidy.

631
00:44:40,678 --> 00:44:42,137
And if we get Jeong-yo,

632
00:44:42,221 --> 00:44:44,306
there will be so many endorsement offers.

633
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:47,768
I can't just let such an opportunity
get away.

634
00:44:49,311 --> 00:44:50,145
Alright?

635
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:18,215
Try it. I heard

636
00:45:18,716 --> 00:45:20,926
this place is popular so I stood in line.

637
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:28,392
Mm. It's really good.

638
00:45:28,475 --> 00:45:29,435
Isn't it?

639
00:45:29,518 --> 00:45:30,352
Am I right?

640
00:45:34,356 --> 00:45:36,066
Mm. It's good.

641
00:45:37,526 --> 00:45:38,360
Mm.

642
00:45:40,028 --> 00:45:41,655
Here, try this one too.

643
00:45:46,034 --> 00:45:49,580
So I complained to the manager of that
venue, "How could you handle things

644
00:45:49,663 --> 00:45:50,497
this way?"

645
00:45:51,373 --> 00:45:53,083
And you know what he said to me?

646
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:57,379
What's wrong? Kang Pi-o.

647
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:00,591
Are you even listening?

648
00:46:01,925 --> 00:46:03,177
Uh… oh,

649
00:46:03,802 --> 00:46:05,888
- of course.
- Uh huh.

650
00:46:05,971 --> 00:46:08,015
I don't think you were listening at all.

651
00:46:09,683 --> 00:46:11,935
Sorry. I'm just a little tired.

652
00:46:12,436 --> 00:46:13,479
That's alright.

653
00:46:14,062 --> 00:46:16,482
I wasn't… saying anything that important.

654
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:18,358
Honestly,

655
00:46:18,901 --> 00:46:21,153
there is one thing that I did want to

656
00:46:21,236 --> 00:46:22,404
talk to you about.

657
00:46:24,031 --> 00:46:24,865
What is it?

658
00:46:25,866 --> 00:46:26,784
Did you hear?

659
00:46:27,868 --> 00:46:28,869
Jeong-yo is going to

660
00:46:29,369 --> 00:46:31,205
join the Hankook Symphony Orchestra.

661
00:46:31,955 --> 00:46:32,790
Did you know?

662
00:46:33,916 --> 00:46:34,750
Oh…

663
00:46:36,084 --> 00:46:37,169
So I guess he took the offer.

664
00:46:37,252 --> 00:46:39,546
Huh? Did you know about that?

665
00:46:41,507 --> 00:46:42,341
So apparently,

666
00:46:43,008 --> 00:46:44,802
Mr. Kang had requested Jeong-yo.

667
00:46:44,885 --> 00:46:46,470
He was the one who wanted him.

668
00:46:46,553 --> 00:46:47,471
And it  sounds like

669
00:46:47,554 --> 00:46:49,097
Jeong-yo also respects him

670
00:46:49,181 --> 00:46:50,808
and wants to work with him, too.

671
00:46:53,018 --> 00:46:53,852
That's great.

672
00:46:54,686 --> 00:46:56,522
- He'll do well.
- I agree.

673
00:46:57,022 --> 00:46:58,440
Isn't that just great?

674
00:46:59,399 --> 00:47:00,234
Mm-hmm.

675
00:47:00,317 --> 00:47:01,485
Then, how would you…

676
00:47:03,695 --> 00:47:05,197
feel about being the soloist

677
00:47:06,365 --> 00:47:07,783
for his very first show?

678
00:47:07,866 --> 00:47:08,826
What do you think?

679
00:47:10,577 --> 00:47:12,746
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Well he's…

680
00:47:13,872 --> 00:47:14,706
he's gonna…

681
00:47:15,582 --> 00:47:17,251
do a concerto anyway…

682
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:19,294
And since he'll need a soloist,

683
00:47:20,003 --> 00:47:20,838
I just figured

684
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:23,090
you could do it if you want to.

685
00:47:23,674 --> 00:47:24,633
- I don't.
- Why not?

686
00:47:24,716 --> 00:47:26,343
I just don't.

687
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:29,888
I don't want to think about performing.

688
00:47:34,476 --> 00:47:36,061
Hey, don't be like that.

689
00:47:37,187 --> 00:47:38,605
Just keep an open mind and

690
00:47:38,689 --> 00:47:39,815
think about it.

691
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:41,483
If you remember,

692
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:44,069
you were always happiest when you
two were

693
00:47:44,152 --> 00:47:45,612
sharing the stage together.

694
00:47:46,154 --> 00:47:47,656
Don't you think it'll be easier

695
00:47:47,739 --> 00:47:49,908
if you work to overcome your issues
together?

696
00:47:49,992 --> 00:47:52,786
So why do I need to work with Jeong-yo
do that?

697
00:47:53,495 --> 00:47:57,165
Do you think I'm so pathetic that I can't
overcome this slump on my own?

698
00:47:57,249 --> 00:47:59,167
You know that's not what it is.

699
00:47:59,251 --> 00:48:00,335
I just  need

700
00:48:01,378 --> 00:48:03,213
a little more time to figure it out.

701
00:48:05,340 --> 00:48:07,509
It's just going to take some time,
alright?

702
00:48:15,058 --> 00:48:16,935
Oh. Mr. Kang!

703
00:48:17,895 --> 00:48:18,979
Oh, Jae-in.

704
00:48:20,272 --> 00:48:21,773
Were you out somewhere?

705
00:48:22,566 --> 00:48:23,400
I just…

706
00:48:23,483 --> 00:48:26,653
dropped by to briefly discuss something
with Pi-o.

707
00:48:26,737 --> 00:48:27,571
Mm, okay.

708
00:48:27,654 --> 00:48:28,488
That's great.

709
00:48:29,865 --> 00:48:31,658
Come inside and let's have some tea.

710
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:32,659
Sorry?

711
00:48:36,997 --> 00:48:37,956
So we meet again.

712
00:48:39,249 --> 00:48:42,461
Hey, I had no idea that you were the
Maestro's grandson.

713
00:48:42,544 --> 00:48:44,713
I heard you were joining the symphony.

714
00:48:45,547 --> 00:48:46,506
That's great.

715
00:48:47,674 --> 00:48:48,926
Let's go inside and talk.

716
00:48:56,850 --> 00:48:59,186
Jeong-yo isn't even Pi-o's competitor
anymore.

717
00:48:59,895 --> 00:49:00,729
Is there

718
00:49:01,730 --> 00:49:03,273
perhaps another reason--

719
00:49:05,525 --> 00:49:07,152
I need to find a way.

720
00:49:08,403 --> 00:49:09,404
There has to be one.

721
00:49:39,977 --> 00:49:41,395
It's not like it used to be.

722
00:49:42,104 --> 00:49:44,064
There are so many ways to market things.

723
00:49:44,147 --> 00:49:47,526
These days, there are so many young
classical music fans.

724
00:49:48,068 --> 00:49:50,487
If we use social media effectively,

725
00:49:51,238 --> 00:49:54,908
I think we can create buzz for the
festival without just relying on TV or

726
00:49:54,992 --> 00:49:56,660
magazine ads.

727
00:50:03,333 --> 00:50:05,377
Oh! Ms. Kang!

728
00:50:11,758 --> 00:50:14,720
I had stopped by to discuss something
with Pi-o,

729
00:50:14,803 --> 00:50:17,931
and Mr. Kang asked me to stay for a cup
of tea.

730
00:50:19,057 --> 00:50:20,475
- Yeah?
- Mm-hmm.

731
00:50:24,521 --> 00:50:25,355
Jeong-yo.

732
00:50:28,525 --> 00:50:29,484
Do I look familiar?

733
00:50:30,527 --> 00:50:31,820
I'm Pi-o's mother.

734
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:37,576
No. I'm sorry.

735
00:50:38,201 --> 00:50:39,036
No, it's okay.

736
00:50:39,119 --> 00:50:40,829
I heard what you went through.

737
00:50:42,497 --> 00:50:44,875
Thankfully, you look like
you're doing well.

738
00:50:44,958 --> 00:50:47,753
Don't just stand there. Either go
upstairs or sit down.

739
00:50:48,378 --> 00:50:50,422
You're making my guests uncomfortable.

740
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:05,687
To think I'd get to see you again.

741
00:51:05,771 --> 00:51:07,397
Truly, what a blessing.

742
00:51:10,567 --> 00:51:12,402
You must have gone through so much.

743
00:51:13,820 --> 00:51:15,781
So how did you lose all your memories?

744
00:51:16,406 --> 00:51:17,365
Can I ask you that?

745
00:51:18,241 --> 00:51:20,118
Uh, well…

746
00:51:21,119 --> 00:51:23,121
I remember waking up in a monastery.

747
00:51:24,456 --> 00:51:26,374
I refused medical treatment so…

748
00:51:27,084 --> 00:51:28,585
a monk who used to be a doctor

749
00:51:28,668 --> 00:51:29,795
treated me on his own.

750
00:51:30,837 --> 00:51:32,089
And… When I woke up, well…

751
00:51:32,172 --> 00:51:33,006
uh…

752
00:51:33,507 --> 00:51:37,302
perhaps it was due to the shock of the
surgery, but I don't remember anything.

753
00:51:37,385 --> 00:51:38,386
Oh, dear.

754
00:51:38,470 --> 00:51:39,805
So that's what happened.

755
00:51:41,765 --> 00:51:44,351
Yet you didn't lose sight and kept
studying music.

756
00:51:44,851 --> 00:51:46,228
How impressive.

757
00:51:51,566 --> 00:51:52,734
The piano. Are you still

758
00:51:52,818 --> 00:51:54,111
finding it difficult?

759
00:51:59,157 --> 00:52:00,575
Given his situation,

760
00:52:01,785 --> 00:52:03,495
do you still want to push ahead?

761
00:52:09,501 --> 00:52:10,335
Oh, Mr. Kang…

762
00:52:10,418 --> 00:52:13,964
So nothing has been officially agreed to
between Pi-o and Jeong-yo yet so I'm

763
00:52:14,047 --> 00:52:15,382
not sure if--

764
00:52:15,465 --> 00:52:17,300
Then we can make it official here.

765
00:52:19,594 --> 00:52:20,428
Kang Pi-o,

766
00:52:21,263 --> 00:52:24,724
your friend says he wants to perform a
concerto with you for his debut.

767
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:26,143
What do you think of that?

768
00:52:32,649 --> 00:52:34,651
I'm afraid this will be too much for him.

769
00:52:34,734 --> 00:52:38,321
I'll recommend another soloist instead
and I'll let you think about it.

770
00:52:39,364 --> 00:52:40,323
I don't know…

771
00:52:40,824 --> 00:52:43,034
I really want to perform with Kang Pi-o.

772
00:52:48,039 --> 00:52:51,168
He traveled all the way across the world
for his friend.

773
00:52:51,668 --> 00:52:53,670
I could care less about his "slump."

774
00:52:53,753 --> 00:52:55,881
I don't want to choose another soloist.

775
00:52:55,964 --> 00:52:59,259
I'd like to perform the concerto
with Kang Pi-o, exactly as Ms. Hong

776
00:52:59,342 --> 00:53:00,177
suggested.

777
00:53:02,596 --> 00:53:04,848
Oh, Pi-o, it's actually just--

778
00:53:06,099 --> 00:53:07,017
What do you think?

779
00:53:08,393 --> 00:53:09,311
Are you not a fan?

780
00:53:10,103 --> 00:53:11,730
I think it'll be a lot of fun.

781
00:53:12,772 --> 00:53:14,149
Thank you for the offer…

782
00:53:15,525 --> 00:53:17,110
but I don't really wanna do it.

783
00:53:22,199 --> 00:53:23,033
I'm sorry, but

784
00:53:23,742 --> 00:53:25,118
I'm going to excuse myself.

785
00:53:38,256 --> 00:53:39,090
Pi-o.

786
00:53:41,843 --> 00:53:42,677
Pi-o.

787
00:53:43,929 --> 00:53:44,763
Just a minute.

788
00:53:45,430 --> 00:53:46,264
Just wait.

789
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:48,934
Hear me out before you go.

790
00:53:49,017 --> 00:53:51,186
So… uh…

791
00:53:52,145 --> 00:53:53,897
I just wanna say I'm sorry.

792
00:53:53,980 --> 00:53:56,024
For talking to Jeong-yo about this first.

793
00:53:56,107 --> 00:53:57,067
But,

794
00:53:57,817 --> 00:54:00,654
I wanted to gauge Jeong-yo's interest
before I tried to convince you.

795
00:54:00,737 --> 00:54:02,906
Why would you ask him about that first?

796
00:54:03,531 --> 00:54:05,200
You should have come to me first.

797
00:54:05,825 --> 00:54:06,660
Well,

798
00:54:07,494 --> 00:54:10,163
that's because I needed to know what
he was thinking…

799
00:54:12,123 --> 00:54:12,958
I'm sorry, Pi-o.

800
00:54:14,292 --> 00:54:15,585
I shouldn't have done that.

801
00:54:15,669 --> 00:54:17,837
- Let's stop this--
- Enough for today.

802
00:54:18,838 --> 00:54:19,714
We'll talk later.

803
00:54:20,882 --> 00:54:21,716
Later.

804
00:54:22,717 --> 00:54:23,551
But…

805
00:54:26,012 --> 00:54:26,846
Pi-o.

806
00:54:58,753 --> 00:54:59,629
I'm really sorry

807
00:54:59,713 --> 00:55:01,464
for making such a mess of things.

808
00:55:02,090 --> 00:55:03,174
Ugh…

809
00:55:03,258 --> 00:55:06,136
I should have seen this coming, shouldn't
I have?

810
00:55:07,387 --> 00:55:09,139
I didn't think it was that serious.

811
00:55:09,889 --> 00:55:10,724
It's okay.

812
00:55:11,599 --> 00:55:13,768
I had a feeling he might react that way.

813
00:55:15,020 --> 00:55:15,854
So…

814
00:55:16,354 --> 00:55:17,355
Does that mean you

815
00:55:17,856 --> 00:55:20,317
- still want to perform with him?
- Of course.

816
00:55:20,817 --> 00:55:21,901
I have to.

817
00:55:23,069 --> 00:55:25,155
Things are even more interesting now.

818
00:55:46,301 --> 00:55:48,219
I'll call you later. Have a good one.

819
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:50,597
Thanks for everything.

820
00:55:51,431 --> 00:55:52,640
Okay. Drive safe.

821
00:55:52,724 --> 00:55:53,683
Mm-hmm.

822
00:56:19,459 --> 00:56:20,293
Hey, hyung.

823
00:56:21,669 --> 00:56:22,545
I just returned.

824
00:56:25,465 --> 00:56:26,299
Where is it?

825
00:56:27,675 --> 00:56:28,718
Oh, there?

826
00:56:29,302 --> 00:56:30,178
Yeah, I recall.

827
00:56:30,261 --> 00:56:31,096
Uh huh.

828
00:56:31,721 --> 00:56:32,722
I'll be right there.

829
00:57:14,806 --> 00:57:16,266
CHOI JEONG-YO

830
00:57:18,643 --> 00:57:22,647
What was even more astonishing was your
unique interpretation of the set piece.

831
00:57:23,189 --> 00:57:26,317
How were you able to accomplish
such a difficult challenge?

832
00:57:26,401 --> 00:57:27,861
I couldn't interpret it.

833
00:57:27,944 --> 00:57:30,405
Even if I go out there, I'll fail at this
rate.

834
00:57:31,614 --> 00:57:34,200
I've already memorized it all.
Use it if you need it!

835
00:57:34,284 --> 00:57:36,119
I just focused on doing the best,

836
00:57:36,828 --> 00:57:38,371
and it led to a good result.

837
00:57:38,455 --> 00:57:39,456
Come to think of it,

838
00:57:39,539 --> 00:57:42,083
you went to the same school as that
competitor, right?

839
00:57:42,167 --> 00:57:43,418
Were you close?

840
00:57:43,918 --> 00:57:47,797
I think I need to enter if I want to
help Pi-o get back on his feet.

841
00:57:48,298 --> 00:57:51,801
If he needs me to be his kindling,
I'd be more than happy to do that

842
00:57:51,885 --> 00:57:52,719
for him.

843
00:57:54,345 --> 00:57:56,598
No, we weren't that close.

844
00:58:12,363 --> 00:58:14,532
- Yes?
- Hello, Mr. Domenico?

845
00:58:15,033 --> 00:58:17,160
I am so sorry to bother you, but

846
00:58:17,660 --> 00:58:22,040
there is someone here who says he's your
friend and that he would like to see you.

847
00:58:22,123 --> 00:58:23,124
A friend?

848
00:58:23,958 --> 00:58:26,294
- Who?
- It's Pi-o Kang.

849
00:58:27,837 --> 00:58:28,671
Pi-o Kang?

850
00:58:29,422 --> 00:58:30,673
I don't know who that is.

851
00:58:38,556 --> 00:58:41,809
I'm truly grateful that you're alive.

852
00:58:41,893 --> 00:58:43,561
Why would you be grateful for that?

853
00:58:43,645 --> 00:58:46,564
Because you were my friend,
and I desperately hoped you were

854
00:58:46,648 --> 00:58:47,732
still alive.

855
00:58:57,534 --> 00:59:00,411
SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK
FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

856
00:59:20,807 --> 00:59:22,559
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

857
00:59:23,059 --> 00:59:25,103
Are you still afraid of being on stage?

858
00:59:25,186 --> 00:59:27,480
Or does the idea of performing with me
make you nervous?

859
00:59:27,564 --> 00:59:31,025
By the way, how much do you actually
remember? And what have you forgotten?

860
00:59:31,109 --> 00:59:33,528
Who was the gentleman playing the piano?
He was pretty good.

861
00:59:33,611 --> 00:59:36,197
What do you think about doing the
concerto together?

862
00:59:36,281 --> 00:59:38,533
Why do you go around telling people
you have amnesia?

863
00:59:38,616 --> 00:59:41,035
You want me to break his fingers for ya?

864
00:59:41,119 --> 00:59:42,370
Where's the fun in that?

865
00:59:42,870 --> 00:59:45,623
Are you really considering performing a
concerto with him?

866
00:59:45,707 --> 00:59:48,960
- Honestly, he doesn't have it.
- Then why don't you perform with me?
